I did in Salisbury Library. he came in. He came gliding in or then he said, hello boys and girls. It was not what we were expecting. No, not at all. So all that summer, as the heat is rising, Calhans ministers are arguing ferociously about the road ahead. On the one hand, Healy says, we're going to have to make these cuts. We're going to have to make them first before the IMF get here.
我在索尔兹伯里图书馆见过。他进来了。他滑了进来，然后他说：“你好，男孩女孩们。”这不是我们所期待的。不，一点也不。所以整个夏天，随着热浪上升，卡拉汉的部长们在未来的道路上争论得非常激烈。一方面，希利说：“我们必须进行这些削减。我们必须在IMF到达之前先进行削减。”

55
