Basically, if we don't make them to appease the markets, the IMF will make them for us. And Healy wants to cut spending by more than a billion pounds, is basically two and a half percent of everybody's budget. Now, a lot of people don't agree, and they are led by our old friend Tony Ben. Are they using the word austerity at this point? Or is that a slogan of a later age? They're not using it. I think they might use it in passing every now and again, but they don't use it quite as much as would be used in the 2010s. It's not as common. But it's basically the same situation, isn't it? It's not a dissimilar situation. Now, Tony Ben says, we don't need to make any cuts at all. He has another idea, which was called
基本上，如果我们不为了安抚市场而进行削减，IMF会为我们进行削减。希利想削减超过10亿英镑的开支，基本上是每个人预算的2.5%。现在，很多人不同意，他们由我们的老朋友托尼·本领导。他们此时在使用“紧缩”（austerity）这个词吗？还是那是后来时代的口号？他们没有使用它。我想他们可能会偶尔顺便提到它，但他们使用的频率不像2010年代那样高。它没那么普遍。但基本上是同样的情况，不是吗？情况并不不同。现在，托尼·本说，我们根本不需要进行任何削减。他有另一个想法，被称为……

