Well, Tony Ben joins us now on the rest of its history. This is exactly what Tony Ben would say. Tony Ben would say the party has just told you to nationalize the four biggest banks. You're in government. You know, you should be doing the bidding of the party. Why are you ignoring the party? And James Callaghan and Dennis Healy would say, I don't care what the party says. We'll do what we're like. That's mad. And this was a constant problem for the Labour Party, and it reaches ahead in the early 1980s when basically Ben and the activists launch a revolution against their own leadership and seize control of the party machinery from them, effectively, at the Labour Party Conference. And they said, not unreasonably, we keep voting for these things, and you just keep ignoring it, and ripping up the manifesto and doing capitalist things.
好吧，托尼·本现在加入了我们的《历史的其余部分》。这正是托尼·本会说的话。托尼·本会说，党刚刚告诉你要将四大银行国有化。你身在政府。你知道，你应该执行党的命令。你为什么要无视党？而吉姆·卡拉汉和丹尼斯·希利会说，我不在乎党怎么说。我们想怎么做就怎么做。这太疯狂了。这对工党来说是一个持续存在的问题，并在20世纪80年代初达到顶峰，当时本和激进分子基本上对他们自己的领导层发动了革命，并在工党大会上有效地从他们手中夺取了党内机器的控制权。他们说，这并非不合理，我们一直在投票支持这些事情，而你们却一直无视它，撕毁宣言，做着资本主义的事情。

